# iOS-only app

`eyefreshAI` ships to iOS only. `app.json` declares `"platforms": ["ios"]`
and there is no web or Android build. Treat iOS as the sole target.

## Do not

- Do not introduce `.web.ts(x)` or `.native.ts(x)` file splits. There is one
  default file per component/hook/lib module.
- Do not branch on `Platform.OS === 'web'` or `'android'`. Delete such checks
  and keep the iOS path only.
- Do not import `react-dom`, `react-native-web`, `next/*`, or any DOM API
  (`window`, `document`, `localStorage`, `navigator.clipboard`, etc.).
- Do not add Android-only settings to `app.json` (no `android`, no
  `androidSpeechServicePackages`, no `android-icon-*` assets).
- Do not add `expo start --web`, `expo run:android`, or `web`/`android`
  scripts to `package.json`.

## Do

- Target the iOS path directly — `SymbolView`, `BlurView`, `expo-blur`,
  `expo-glass-effect`, iOS shadow props (`shadowColor`/`shadowOpacity`/
  `shadowRadius`/`shadowOffset`), etc.
- Use `Platform.OS === 'ios'` only when a library legitimately requires it
  (e.g. `KeyboardAvoidingView` behavior). Prefer writing iOS-only values
  directly.
- Native permissions strings live in `app.json` under `ios.infoPlist`.

## Persistence

- Chat history uses `expo-sqlite` (see `src/lib/chat/chat-repository.ts`).
  Do not add a `localStorage`/`AsyncStorage` fallback "for web".
- File paths for attachments use `expo-file-system` (`documentDirectory`).

## Sign-in

- Supabase OAuth uses `expo-web-browser` (`openAuthSessionAsync`) — never
  `window.location` or `signInWithOAuth` browser redirects.
